      "title": "Agreed order scope",
      "text": "Order form agreed by Nkem of Woven Creek Studio, Nigeria, and buyer Lora Vale.\n\nDeliver 12 handloom cotton scarves in indigo.\nDeliver 12 handloom cotton scarves in sand.\nUse natural plant dyes for all 24 scarves.\nInclude a printed care card with each scarf.\n\nPrice: USD 288 for the scarves and USD 32 for shipping, payable through PayPal. The scarves are intended for Lora's small retail display. Nkem will pack the two colors separately and send the parcel by DHL Express. Lora approved this scope before Nkem started weaving; no gift wrapping was requested."
    },
    {
      "title": "Delivery handover note",
      "text": "Woven Creek Studio handover note, prepared by Nkem for Lora Vale.\n\nPacked: 12 handloom cotton scarves in indigo; 8 handloom cotton scarves in sand. A printed care card was placed with each of the 20 scarves. The remaining four sand scarves were not packed because they were not ready. Nkem told Lora that the shortfall would need a separate arrangement.\n\nThe parcel was handed to DHL Express with invented tracking number JD7A4B2C9D6E3F1G. DHL Express delivery record: delivered to Lora's reception desk. This note records the contents counted at packing; it does not include dye purchase records or a dye specification."
    },
    {
      "title": "Chat after delivery",
      "text": "10:12 Lora: The parcel reached my reception desk this morning. I counted 12 indigo and eight sand scarves.\n\n10:16 Nkem: Thanks for checking. I'm sorry the four remaining sand scarves weren't in the parcel. Can we arrange a separate shipment?\n\n10:20 Lora: Let's discuss that tomorrow. Each scarf I received had its care card tucked inside.\n\n10:24 Nkem: Good. I have your count noted down.\n\n10:29 Lora: I'll keep the packaging until we settle the missing pieces. The colors look consistent across the scarves I received.\n\n10:32 Nkem: Understood. I'll message you with an update on the four sand scarves."
    }
